@meta
  v: 1
  route: /
  generated: 2026-09-09T00:00:00+05:30
  ttl: 1d

@intent
  purpose: Make the supplied distributed pharmacy RMI system inspectable through a scroll-led control room.
  audience: project-reviewer, distributed-systems-learner, pharma-operations-partner
  capability: observe, search, inspect

@state
  page_state: ready
  opening_sequence: live WebGL cluster (three.js), scroll moves the camera, time keeps the protocol running
  scene_chapters: router fan-out, bully election, primary-backup failover, vector clocks + OCC, SHA-256 prescription chain
  data_mode: read-only + simulated fault lab
  gateway: java-http-api
  collections: branches, medicines, prescriptions, inventory, transactions
  fault_tolerance: primary-backup simulation, ephemeral
  reduced_motion: supported
  language: en

@actions
  - id: skip_opening
    method: GET
    href: /#overview
  - id: view_network
    method: GET
    href: /#network
  - id: inspect_data
    method: GET
    href: /#explorer
  - id: inspect_protocol
    method: GET
    href: /#protocol
  - id: open_fault_lab
    method: GET
    href: /#fault-tolerance
  - id: simulate_primary_failure
    method: POST
    href: /api/fault-tolerance/action?action=fail-primary
  - id: open_integrity
    method: GET
    href: /#integrity
  - id: recover_primary
    method: POST
    href: /api/fault-tolerance/action?action=recover-primary

@context
  > A monochrome distributed-pharmacy control room. One persistent WebGL canvas renders the six-node cluster into five scene windows: router fan-out, bully election, failover, vector clocks, and a SHA-256 prescription chain in which prescription 017 fails verification (client-side model).
  > The Java gateway projects the PostgreSQL dataset (helixis_pharmacy) and probes six RMI registries. The pharmacy data remains read-only; the fault lab exposes only an ephemeral primary-backup simulation with failover and replay evidence.

@nav
  self: /index.agent
  parents: [/]
  peers: [/index.html]
  drilldown: /#explorer
